  "description": "DDoS analysis over NetFlow. This is forensics and visibility, not detection: sampling (typically 1:100) and a one-minute active flow timeout mean small attacks are statistically invisible and everything lags by a minute or two. Keep a scrubbing appliance as the detector. Mean packet size, shown next to PPS, is the cheapest discriminator between a packet flood and an amplification attack.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 301,
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "html",
        "content": "<div style=\"text-align:center;padding:16px 0 6px;font-family:Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><div style=\"font-size:38px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:3px;color:#e9eef5;line-height:1\">DDoS &mdash; ANALYSIS</div><div style=\"margin-top:10px;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:5px;color:#8b98a9;text-transform:uppercase\">Traffic shape, targets and attack signature</div><div style=\"margin:15px auto 0;width:220px;height:2px;border-radius:2px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(79,163,255,0),#4FA3FF,rgba(79,163,255,0))\"></div></div>",
